+-## Rev0666 changes
++## Rev0667 changes
+ 
+-- Adds `SyncChunkResponseBatchEnvelope` to carry request ID, batch ID, remote entry/version digests, apply intent ID, response count, total response bytes, and the ordered response envelopes included in the peer batch.
+-- Adds `build_sync_chunk_response_batch_envelope` to construct deterministic `sync-chunk-response-batch:v1:` evidence only for ordered unique subsets of a valid `sync-chunk-request:v1:` batch.
+-- Adds `SyncChunkResponseBatchAcceptanceResult` to report batch-level request/batch verification, written chunk count, reused receipt count, completion state, and per-chunk acceptance evidence.
+-- Adds `accept_sync_chunk_response_batch_envelope` to rebuild request evidence, rebuild and compare the expected batch envelope, prevalidate byte length/hash for every response, and then route each response through `accept_sync_chunk_response_envelope` and the receipt-backed staged writer.
+-- Extends `--selftest-sync-domain-model` with duplicate-batch rejection, valid two-response batch construction, forged-batch-ID rejection, and batch acceptance that completes a staged transfer from reusable middle-chunk receipt plus two peer responses.
+-- Adds rev0666 docs, audit record, source patch, validator, build/test logs, active binary, and package manifest.
++- Adds `SyncChunkTransferRoundResult` to carry batch acceptance evidence, post-batch staged-transfer inspection, the next chunk request plan, and ready/continuation flags.
++- Adds `accept_sync_chunk_response_batch_and_plan_next` to accept a batch response, re-inspect receipt-backed staging state, and deterministically build the next request plan from the verified post-write state.
++- Rejects mismatched write and inspection roots before accepting peer bytes, preventing a session caller from writing into one staging tree and deriving continuation evidence from another.
++- Extends `--selftest-sync-domain-model` with a two-round, four-chunk transfer: first batch writes two chunks and emits a continuation request; second batch completes the staged file and marks it ready to materialize.
++- Keeps the C++ transfer boundary local and deterministic; no real network/session scheduler is claimed yet.
++- Adds rev0667 docs, audit record, source patch, validator, build/test logs, active binary, and package manifest.
